#import "main-defs.typ": *
#import "statements.typ": *

= Orders <ch:orders>

#source(117)Throughout this chapter let $R$ denote a noetherian integral domain
with quotient field $K$, and let $A$ be a finite dimensional $K$-algebra. Our
aim here is to define orders, and to develop some of their basic properties. In
later chapters we shall concentrate on maximal orders. Usually $R$ will be a
Dedekind domain, or at the very least, an integrally closed domain (see
@def:integrally-closed), but occasionally theorems will be stated for the
general situation in which $R$ is only assumed to be noetherian.
